-- title:
--   Existence of a lift along a small extension
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation domain $W_0$ which is $\mathfrak m$-adically complete and whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjective ring map $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative one-dimensional formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. with the ideal structure given by $\bot$ there is a unit $u \in k[[X]]$ with $F_0.\mathrm{nthSeries}\ q = u \cdot F_0.\mathrm{drinfeldDivisor}\ q\ 0\ 0$, and let $F_u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[[X]]$ whose two-variable power series maps, under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, to that of $F_0$. Assume the universal property `hFu1`: for every artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T'$ with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_{T'} : T' \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, such that $\mathfrak m_{T'}^2 = 0$ and $q = 0$ in $T'$, and every commutative formal group law $G'$ over $T'$ whose base change along $\mathrm{res}_{T'}$ is $F_0$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to T'$ with $\mathrm{res}_{T'} \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ admitting a formal group law over $T'$ which is the base change of $F_u$ along $\varphi$ and an isomorphism of laws from it to $G'$ whose series has $n$-th coefficient reducing to $1$ for $n = 1$ and to $0$ otherwise. Now let $T$ and $S$ be artinian local $W_0$-algebras with surjections $\mathrm{res}_T, \mathrm{res}_S$ onto $k$ with kernel the maximal ideal, $\mathrm{res}_T$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, and let $\sigma : T \to S$ be a surjective $W_0$-algebra map with $\mathrm{res}_S \circ \sigma = \mathrm{res}_T$ which is small in the sense $(\ker \sigma) \cdot \mathfrak m_T = \bot$. Let $G$ be a commutative formal group law over $T$ base-changing to $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, let $G_\sigma$ over $S$ be the base change of $G$ along $\sigma$, and let $\bar\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to S$ be a $W_0$-algebra map with $\mathrm{res}_S \circ \bar\varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ for which the base change $\bar G'$ of $F_u$ along $\bar\varphi$ admits an isomorphism of laws $\bar\psi : \bar G' \to G_\sigma$ (a power series with zero constant term, unit linear coefficient, intertwining the two laws) whose coefficients reduce to $\delta_{n,1}$ in $k$. The conclusion is that some $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to T$ satisfies $\sigma \circ \varphi = \bar\varphi$ and admits a formal group law $G'$ over $T$ which is the base change of $F_u$ along $\varphi$ together with an isomorphism of laws $\psi : G' \to G$ whose $n$-th coefficient reduces to $1$ if $n = 1$ and to $0$ otherwise. No square-zero or $q = 0$ condition is imposed on $T$ itself; those occur only inside the hypothesis `hFu1`.
--
--   This is the existence half of the Schlessinger-style smoothness step for the deformation functor of a height-two formal group law with Drinfeld basis data: a deformation over the quotient $S$, given with its identification with a base change of the universal law $F_u$ over $W_0[[X]]$, is shown to come from such data over $T$ along a small extension $T \to S$. It is used by the combined existence-and-uniqueness statement [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.existsUnique_algHom_powerSeries_lift_of_smallExtension_of_sqZero`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.existsUnique_algHom_powerSeries_lift_of_smallExtension_of_sqZero).
